  "scope": [
    "Same owned-array counter model at8/256/4096/65536bytes for direct consumer transition versus full MemoryMachine publication. Separate owned-copy-and-counter control.",
    "Effect type Infallible, capacity0, trivial model validation, always-accepted event. This isolates a minimal pure state path; flat/hierarchy/intent benchmarks remain independent broader profiles.",
    "Black-box input/output whole arrays; independent closed-form counter and every-word checks outside timing. Kernel additionally checks exact revision and no pending intents.",
    "All allocation/reallocation/deallocation/requested-byte counts zero. Separate positive control requires one allocation and deallocation of16bytes.",
    "No changes to portable production source, publication, validation, recovery, wire or authority rules; no new library dependencies or Clone bounds."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Batch-mean quantiles, not individual-operation tail latency. Very short8byte controls approach timer/loop resolution.",
    "Direct consumer/control paths provide no kernel publication or validation guarantee and are not interchangeable application APIs. Measurements are reported separately; no subtraction or normalization is claimed as isolated kernel overhead.",
    "Compiler may optimize redundant copies and enum plumbing; measures resulting optimized paths, not mandated physical copy counts.",
    "Fixed profile order, short runs on shared host with ongoing disjoint-core chaos campaign. Frequency, caches, thermals and unrelated activity uncontrolled. No cross-compiler speed claim, confidence interval or release acceptance.",
    "Guard/intent/hierarchy dispatch, timeline-over-machine, durable machine SQLite and native end-to-end performance are outside this measurement; remaining release gates stay open."
  ],
